<main>
<article>
<div class="quiet-meta">
<ul class="quiet-tags" aria-label="Tags">
<li>#garden</li>
<li>#notes/rust</li>
</ul>
</div>
<h1 id="the-garden">The garden<a class="quiet-anchor" href="#the-garden" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>
</h1>
<p>A vault read as Obsidian reads it. Links by name <a href="/notes/rust">Rust</a>, in any case <a href="/notes/rust">rust</a>, through an
alias <a href="/notes/rust">the language</a>, by a partial path <a href="/notes/ownership">Notes/Ownership</a>, to a heading
<a href="/notes/rust#borrowing">Rust &gt; Borrowing</a> and to a block <a href="/notes/rust#borrow-rule">Rust &gt; ^borrow-rule</a>. #notes/rust #garden</p>
<details class="quiet-callout quiet-tip">
<summary class="quiet-label">Folded at first</summary>
<p>With <a href="/notes/ownership">Ownership</a> inside.</p>
</details>
<aside class="quiet-callout">
<p class="quiet-label">Questions</p>
<p>Asked often.</p>
</aside>
<p>The borrowing section of another note, embedded:</p>
<div class="quiet-embed">
<h2 id="borrowing">Borrowing<a class="quiet-anchor" href="#borrowing" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>
</h2>
<p>One mutable borrow or many shared ones. </p>
<p>See <a href="/notes/rust#borrowing">Borrowing</a> and the <a href="/notes/ownership">Ownership</a> note.</p>
</div>
<p>One block of it:</p>
<div class="quiet-embed">
<p>One mutable borrow or many shared ones. </p>
</div>
<p>A photo shared by two folders, taken from the attachment folder:</p>
<p>
<picture>
<source type="image/avif" srcset="/attachments/ferris.48.57c8b5bffee92ff9.avif 48w" sizes="(min-width: 42rem) 40rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)">
<img src="/attachments/ferris.48.5b6cb8cacc12719c.png" srcset="/attachments/ferris.48.5b6cb8cacc12719c.png 48w" sizes="(min-width: 42rem) 40rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)" width="48" height="32" alt="ferris.png" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
</picture>
</p>
<p>An embed inside a line, see </p>
<div class="quiet-embed">
<h2 id="borrowing-1">Borrowing<a class="quiet-anchor" href="#borrowing-1" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>
</h2>
<p>One mutable borrow or many shared ones. </p>
<p>See <a href="/notes/rust#borrowing">Borrowing</a> and the <a href="/notes/ownership">Ownership</a> note.</p>
</div>
<p> shown between its text. A single ~tilde~ pair
stays as written, <s>struck</s> is struck, and <code>~code~</code> is code.</p>
<p>A paragraph with its own id. <span id="own">
</span>
</p>
</article>
</main>
<footer class="quiet-foot">
<p>The garden</p>
</footer>
</div>
